  "lineage": "Solomon Islands panpipe ensemble tradition of the Are'are people of southern Malaita island and adjacent Solomons communities, featuring large coordinated ensembles of stopped-bamboo-pipes-arranged-in-rafts played in interlocking hocketed polyphonic patterns. The au tahana (raft-panpipe) and au kuita (bundle-panpipe) instrumental categories support distinct repertoire layers. Performance contexts span feast-day celebrations, mourning-rituals, and (post-1978 independence) international-festival and recording-circuit work through the canonical Narasirato Pan Pipers ensemble formed in the 1990s. The genre is one of the most internationally circulated Melanesian musical traditions through twentieth-century ethnomusicological recording.",
